  "id": "Compound::DB00456 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Cefalotin is shown to interact with Slc22a6 through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve the sodium-independent organic anion transporter activity. The evidence suggests that Cefalotin binds to Slc22a8, which is a component of the organic anion transport system, and this interaction is further linked to Slc22a6 through a participatory relationship. This implies that Cefalotin may influence the function of Slc22a6, potentially by modulating its activity in transporting anions across cellular membranes. The similarity between Cefalotin and Cefazolin, which is also shown to bind to Slc22a6, further supports the notion that Cefalotin may exert a similar effect on Slc22a6. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Cefalotin could affect Slc22a6, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence suggests a direct or indirect influence of Cefalotin on Slc22a6, supported by a chain of molecular interactions that span multiple biological processes.",
